554-
555-**Measured.**
556-
557-- The 16-slot census, correlation matrix, per-slot R², rank and conditioning, on
558-  176,223 shipped rows over 180 anchors and both training worlds, and
559:  independently on 87,997 rows regenerated here for world 1 (exactly the count
560-  the production manifest records for that world).
561-- That 100% of the shipped rows carry the fallback path's forecast-method digest,
562-  proved from the shipped bytes rather than inferred from the flag.
563-- Exact functional dependence between every slot pair, separated from the
564-  artifact of a near-injective determiner.
565:- The per-anchor cost of both row paths on the same anchor: 4.79 s versus
566:  632.83 s.
567-- Field-by-field agreement and disagreement between a fallback row and a normal
568-  row for the same anchor, user and action identity.
569-- The spread of the elevation primitive that no slot carries, over the same
570-  candidate rows.
571-
572-**Not measured, explicitly.**
573-
574-- **A both-ways diff over all 180 anchors.** The normal path costs 433-633 s per
575-  anchor, so the full grid is roughly 24-31 hours single-threaded; that was out of
576-  reach here. The mechanical diff covers **2 of 180 anchors** (steps 0 and 15 on
577:  world 1, carrier `nearest-eligible`), and the code-read table covers the rest.
578-  I have not substituted a proxy for the unmeasured anchors — the field table is
579-  labelled as a code read, and every count in the measured tables is per-anchor,
580-  not extrapolated. Two anchors establish that each divergence *can* occur and
581-  did; they do not establish its corpus-wide rate.
582-- **Whether the normal path's own C1/C2 targets are correct.** I established only
--
584-  audit does not validate the normal path.
585-- **The rekey-active branch of Φ.** Every anchor on both training tapes carries
586-  dense arrays (30/30 checked on world 1), so `_rekeyed_users` returns empty
587-  everywhere and the omitted argument cannot be exercised on this corpus at all.
588-  Defect B4 is therefore reported as latent on evidence, not as active.
589:- **ψ for differently-selected coalitions beyond the diffed anchors.** The
590:  coalition row's ψ is computed from real physics on both paths; what differs is
591:  which coalition is selected and that its member feature vectors are fallback Q1
592-  rows. I measured the identity difference, not the resulting ψ distribution
593-  across the corpus.
594-- **The heads' internal input handling.** I read `_route_state` and found no
595-  rescaling of `q1_state` before it reaches a head, so the conditioning numbers
596-  are as-consumed; I did not trace initialisation or any per-layer normalisation
