codex
The calibration loop will assert the exact symptom—the two published rates disagree by about an order of magnitude—and record row counts plus physical-evaluation counts so timing alone cannot mislead us.

Ranked hypotheses before measurement:

1. `include_coalition=True` is the main cause of the 632.83/4.79 configuration; it adds catalogue construction and evaluation absent from the 49.03/0.848 configuration.
2. The 632.83 figure includes cold full-tape/module work or contention that the newer row-only benchmark excluded.
3. “All three carriers” changes total anchor count, not intrinsic per-anchor work; carrier identity may cause smaller row-count/runtime variation.
4. Boundary policy is not the differentiator because both prior records appear to use the one-boundary `(0,)` dense path.
5. Warm caches affect timing modestly but cannot explain a 10–13× exact-path gap if physical-evaluation counts are comparable.

I’ll test the first four on four distinct anchors, with a repeat for warm-cache sensitivity.
