+# Exact source build completion criterion
+
+The task is complete when a four-anchor, both-path calibration reconciles the
+published timing discrepancy; the Part 1 reconciliation is printed before any
+generation begins; and the new exact-path artefact contains a clean prefix of
+the predeclared 180-anchor order, per-anchor checkpoints, an independently
+verified manifest, and the required C1 gauge, decomposition, correlation,
+rank-correlation, and argmax-disagreement measurements, without changing the
+pilot runner bytes or any sealed input.

codex
Calibration is running with four Python workers. Each anchor uses fresh evaluators on a four-step tape; tape construction is timed separately and excluded from the reconciled per-anchor rate. One worker also measures the coalition-enabled configuration and repeats the exact no-coalition build to expose warm-cache effects.
